<title>SOUTH AFRICA: De Beers plans 4.3 bln yen Japan promotion.</title>
<headline>De Beers plans 4.3 bln yen Japan promotion.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diamond giant De Beers said on Thursday it would spend around 4.3 billion yen on its Japanese marketing budget this year in a bid to boost sales.</p>
<p>The investment was intended to provide even stronger support to the group's five fields - market and consumer research, advertising, publicity and promotion and education for the diamond jewellery industry, De Beers said a statement.</p>
<p>Japan is the second largest diamond market in the world after the United States.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
